Ticket #4471 merged **412 reports** (the export has 427 rows; 15 are repeats of the same id).
Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put three
different problems into one ticket. They are split below by tenant locale, booking form and
body text, using the logic in `causes.ts`, not by the intake tag.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Three problems, three fixes. The "one fix queued" does not cover 38 of the 412 reports.
</Callout>

| Problem | Reports | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `parser` | 374 | The shared parser reads dates month first. Day-first tenants (all 11 on file) see month and day swapped. |
| `hint` | 33 | booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. People at day-first tenants (copper.studio, alder.physio, pale.harbour) type month first through the form, and the form reads it day first. A different bug: the fix is the hint text, not the parser. |
| `one-day move` | 5 | The date is off by exactly one day, not swapped (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620). Reports point at a time zone problem, not at parsing. The desk had filed them under `parser`. |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412.

## Notes

- Intake tags are a guess from the reporter's browser: of the 33 `hint` reports, 15 were tagged `parser`; 23 `hint`-tagged reports belong to `parser`.
- Four reports (R-41290, R-41417, R-41514, R-41615) give no usable date. They stay in `parser` by tenant; confirm when the parser fix ships.
- Merging "when unsure" ([triage: duplicates](/kb/triage/dedupe)) is what hid this. Match on cause (tenant locale + booking form), not on subject.

## Lessons

- A big ticket can be several bugs reported many times. Split by cause before you count.
- Count unique ids first: exports overlap.

